I built the issue desk as one app machine (in `src/appMachine.ts`) that invokes a separate actor for each page, so leaving a page stops it and drops any answers still on the way. The issues page has a child actor per selected issue, and every optimistic change (assign, rename, close, posts, labels, saves) runs as its own `fromPromise` request actor tagged with a sequence number, so a decline rolls back only that change and a late or out-of-order answer can't undo a newer one; `./check` passes and `./test` passes 30/30. I wasn't sure about a few choices the brief leaves open: the detail's assign error shows only the server's message, `title-input` keeps its text after a rename, search results are cleared when a search fails, and the assign buttons are disabled while the user name is blank.